WUU2 — Windows Update Utility (GUI Edition)
===========================================

This software is an evolved derivative work based upon multiple open-source
PowerShell patch management utilities. All upstream projects and this derivative
work are released under the terms of the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Upstream Lineage & Copyright Attribution:
------------------------------------------

1. PoshPAIG (PowerShell Patch Audit/Installation GUI)
   - Initial Release: 2011; GitHub repository established 2014
   - Author: Boe Prox
   - Original Repository: CodePlex (poshpaig.codeplex.com) / GitHub (https://github.com/proxb/PoshPAIG)
   - Copyright: Copyright (c) 2014 Boe Prox
   - Key contributions retained/descended:
     * Synchronized runspace collection architecture ($jobs, $jobCleanup, $updatesHash)
     * Host exclusion list handling (Exempt.txt)
     * Administrative elevation check patterns
     * Remote patch check and installation workflow concepts

2. Windows Update Utility (WUU)
   - Release: December 14, 2016
   - Author: Tyler Siegrist
   - Publication: Microsoft TechNet / Script Center (ID 1d72e520) / GitHub (https://github.com/HashGambit97/WindowsUpdateUtility)
   - Attribution: Documented as a major architectural rewrite of PoshPAIG
   - Copyright: Copyright (c) 2016 Tyler Siegrist
   - Key contributions retained/descended:
     * Consolidation into unified automation scriptblocks ($GetUpdates, $DownloadUpdates, $InstallUpdates)
     * Native Windows Update Agent (WUA) COM API automation (Microsoft.Update.Session)
     * WPF/XAML interface design (WUU.xaml, OUPicker.xaml)
     * Update search query criteria ("IsInstalled=0 and IsHidden=0") and local install loops

3. WUU2
   - Initial Release: October 2018
   - Maintainer: HanSolo71
   - Forum Contributor: Phaere
   - Repository: GitHub (https://github.com/HanSolo71/WUU2)
   - Copyright: Copyright (c) 2018 HanSolo71
   - Key contributions retained/descended:
     * Runspace scope isolation and stability fixes
     * Formal publication under the MIT License on GitHub

4. WUU2 (GUI Edition)
   - Development: 2025–2026
   - Author: dazzo31
   - Repository: https://github.com/dazzo31/WUU2
   - Copyright: Copyright (c) 2025-2026 dazzo31
   - Key architectural enhancements and new implementations:
     * Removal of PsExec dependency in favour of temporary SYSTEM scheduled tasks
     * 5-wave phased deployment engine with automated phase gates
     * Multi-target custom credential isolation via DCOM CIM sessions
     * Hardened timeout budgets, deadline floors, and heartbeat monitoring
     * Thread deadlock fixes across UI dispatcher and worker runspaces
     * WSUS audit tool integration (Audit-WSUSUpdates.ps1)

For complete details on the migration and code transformation, see docs/PROVENANCE.md.